From 93eb3cf545d7ab1af9b5fbad6c700ae2b2b0290b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:14:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 254/288] Unified: applying the network settings never waits
 (froze for minutes on Windows)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Report: Edit > Preferences > General > Network, manual proxy localhost:8083
(nothing listening), Apply -> the whole window "not responding" for several
minutes with no CPU and no connection, then it recovered.

Cause: apply_qt_proxy() put Qt on "system proxy configuration" (the default
mode and at every start). On Windows every Qt proxy lookup then runs WinHTTP
auto-detection (WPAD), which takes minutes on a company network, and Qt holds
its global proxy lock while it does. Apply calls setApplicationProxy() on the
GUI thread, which waits for that lock. (Checked with Qt 6.11: a slow proxy
factory in another thread blocks setApplicationProxy on the main thread.)
Apply also waited up to 3 s for the AI chat helper to stop, and opening the
preferences waited up to 60 s for the key-store check.

What changed (network/AI files only):
- NetworkSettings: system_proxy() reads only environment variables and, on
  Windows, the manual Internet Options in the registry (the
  WinHttpGetIEProxyConfigForCurrentUser values); no getproxies(), no WPAD,
  no PAC. New check(): connects to the proxy (or directly) with a 5 s timeout
  and asks for CONNECT api.anthropic.com:443; answers in plain Japanese
  (refused / no answer in 5 s / name not found / 407 / OK).
- UnifiedPreferences: apply_qt_proxy() never turns on Qt's system
  configuration; it uses the proxy NetworkSettings.apply() decided. The page
  runs check() in a thread after Apply and shows the result under the proxy
  settings (e.g. "プロキシ localhost:8083 に接続できません（接続を拒否されました…）").
  A Windows PAC-only setup is reported instead of being evaluated.
  The AI chat page checks for a stored key without waiting.
- AIChatGui: restart() closes the helper's input and kills it 3 s later from
  a timer instead of waitForFinished on the GUI thread; has_key_async().
- TestNetworkSettings (FreeCADCmd -t TestNetworkSettings): apply with a
  closed port, a black hole (10.255.255.1:8080), system and no proxy returns
  in < 1 s with no socket/DNS/getproxies call on the main thread and Qt not
  on system configuration; check() messages; a 20 ms heartbeat timer keeps
  running while the check waits on the black hole.

Measured in the GUI (offscreen, AI helper replaced by a process that does not
exit): before, Apply took 3.0 s and Qt was left on system configuration;
after, 0.002 s, longest heartbeat gap 0.07 s, results shown after 0.0 s
(refused) and 5.0 s (black hole).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
